<title>CHINA: China PICC premiums up 40 pct in first quarter.</title>
<headline>China PICC premiums up 40 pct in first quarter.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The People's Insurance Company (Group) of China (PICC) recorded income from premiums of 17.55 billion yuan ($2.11 billion) in January to March, up 40 percent compared with same year-ago period, the Financial News said on Friday.</p>
<p>Of the total, life insurance premiums soared by 102 percent compared with the year-ago period, it said.</p>
<p>The company paid a total of 4.29 billion yuan in claims with payment ratio at 39.49 percent in the first three months, it said.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
